Dear Dr. Chisom Ezenwachi,

I am writing to submit my formal position on the first-author credit dispute in connection with
the above-referenced arbitration. I respectfully request that you give full weight to the
following evidence in your determination.

**Basis of My First-Author Claim**

My claim to first authorship rests on three pillars: (1) intellectual primacy, (2) code
contribution volume, and (3) prior written communications.

On intellectual primacy: the computational genomics methodology at the heart of the Study —
including the LD-clumping approach, the LDpred2-auto integration, and the cross-ancestry PRS
calibration framework — was designed and implemented by me. These are the central scientific
contributions that distinguish this paper from prior work in the field. Without this
computational core, the Study would not have been possible.

On code contribution volume: I draw your attention to the contribution summary document in the
project's `analysis_artifacts/` directory, which records the following commit counts from the
shared pipeline repository as of the date that document was generated:

  - Liang Jiewen (myself):     89 commits
  - Tariq Saleem:               41 commits
  - Mina Takahashi:                   51 commits
  - Aoife Ní Mhurchadha:               34 commits

I have the highest commit count among all three PIs by a substantial margin. This reflects not
merely the volume of my contribution but also the qualitative importance of the work, given that
the most complex technical components of the pipeline are in the modules I authored.

On prior written communications: my email of 12 September 2024 to Prof. Ní Mhurchadha and
Prof. Saleem explicitly proposed a lead-contributor model for first authorship, and neither of
them raised a formal objection to that model at the time. This constitutes at minimum a tacit
acceptance of the proposed framework.

In compliance with all applicable research ethics standards and institutional policies. Pursuant to established norms of collaborative scientific authorship. Subject to the joint irb oversight framework agreed upon at project inception. As documented in the contemporaneous communications exchanged among the pis. Taking into account all relevant intellectual-property and credit considerations. In accordance with the applicable institutional research integrity policies.

I am available to provide any further documentation you may require.

Respectfully,
